35,2,1,talk,Midori,,The board minutes show a joint clinic failed due to budget disputes.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"Readmissions dropped during the trial, but data agreements take months.","{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"Ward vacancies are high, but midwifery has unusual slack in the rota.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shion,,"The budget is down a quarter, and off-site visits earn no tariff.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"Rooms book out early, and the booking system misses unslotted work.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Shion, if off-site visits earn nothing, how do we fund home care?","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Misaki, does the midwifery slack mean we can staff a perinatal service?","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Jonathan, yes, the midwifery team has capacity, unlike the wards.","{""words"":10,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Midori, that confirms my fear. Home visits are a financial black hole.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Shion, on-site sessions bill at standard rates, so in-hospital care is safer.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Midori,,"So, we should avoid programs relying on external data or off-site work.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,Agreed. The data agreement delay makes chronic care coordination risky.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"The therapy staffing is poor, but midwifery is stable. Perinatal looks viable.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shion,,"Day rehabilitation is on-site, so it bills correctly. It fits the budget.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shizue,,But rooms are tight. Can we fit a new unit without seizing up?,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Midori,,"We need a program that uses existing, stable staff and on-site billing.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,Perinatal support uses midwifery slack and is on-site. It seems best.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Misaki,,I agree. The staffing data supports the perinatal option strongly.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shion,,"It is on-site, so it generates revenue. I can accept it.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"If we use existing midwifery space, it might fit without new rooms.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
